  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 143 PM EDT Mon Oct 19 2026\n\nPattern Synopsis/Forecast: Omega block in the process of developing \nacross the central CONUS with upper low anchors off of both coasts \n-- one off the coast of NC/VA and the other off the coast of the Pac \nNW, sagging east off the coast of CA by Tuesday morning. Locally, \nzonal to weakly ridged upper level pattern expected early this week \nbefore ridging becomes more amplified by mid-late week. At the \nsurface, high pressure dominates with an active northern stream \nacross northern Canada simply too far removed from having much of an \nimpact on our sensible weather.\n\nForecast Details: A remarkably tranquil and mild stretch of mid-late \nOctober on tap this week. Daily high temperatures expected to be a \ngood 5-10+ degrees above normal each day, ranging from the upper 50s \nto low 60s across the eastern U.P. and through the 60s south of the \nbridge. Certainly within the realm of possibilities that a handful \nof locations in northern lower tag 70 degrees at times this week. \nOvernight lows largely spanning the mid-30s to mid-40s each night.\n\nAs has been alluded to, a dry forecast is featured this week as well. \nThat said, not without a couple of features to monitor. This first \non Wednesday as a fast-moving shortwave may dive south across the \nnorthern Lakes. Latest trends favor this to be dry, but may bring an \nuptick in cloud cover to the eastern U.P. Wednesday afternoon. Next \nshot for some rain maybe late in the weekend into early next week as \nblocking breaks down, but certainly not a lot of confidence at this \npoint.",
